        "content": "<ul><li><strong>The North:</strong> plain and old: Rickard, Benjen, Lyanna. Northern houses sound cold and hard.</li><li><strong>The Westerlands:</strong> polished and proud, the Lannisters' country: Tywin, Kevan, Cersei.</li><li><strong>The Reach:</strong> courtly and flowery, home of the Tyrells: Mace, Loras, Margaery.</li><li><strong>Dorne:</strong> a different flavour altogether, after the Rhoynar who settled there: Oberyn, Doran, Arianne, Nymeria.</li><li><strong>The Iron Islands:</strong> harsh and salty: Balon, Euron, Asha.</li><li><strong>Valyrian:</strong> the Targaryens' names, full of ae and y: Aegon, Rhaegar, Daenerys, Viserys.</li><li><strong>The Free Folk:</strong> one name, often with an <a href=\"epithet-generator.html\">epithet</a> earned beyond the Wall: Tormund Giantsbane.</li></ul>"
